On Fri, Feb 20, 2015 at 8:32 AM, Erik Natanael Gustafsson <
eriknatanaelgustafsson@gmail.com> wrote:
>
> OK. So either
> .i la .erik. pu farlu ri'a lo bolci be lo rokci ca lo nu ra ca'o klama
> or
> .i la .erik. pu farlu ri'a lo bolci be lo rokci .i ca bo ra ca'o klama
> ?
>

The first one is:

  In the past:
    Caused by the marble:
       At the time he was going:
          Eric falls.

The second one is:

  In the past:
     Caused by the marble:
         Eric falls.
  At the same time:
     He was going.

If you don't want the simultaneity to be part of what is caused, which
makes a subtle difference, you would need to change the order in the first
one: "la .erik pu farlu ca lo nu ri ca'o klama kei ri'a lo bolci be lo
rokci":

  In the past:
     At the time of his going:
        Caused by the marble:
            Eric falls.

mu'o mi'e xorxes

